# A pair of Joy-Cons that SDL takes apart and puts together again
# (ADR-0002), each time with a key held and its ButtonUp lost. The pair
# holds east; R is switched off, SDL deletes the pair and finds L again at
# its next scan, 10 ms later, with a new id: the pair's removal releases
# Space at @500. L taps south, then holds east when R wakes again: SDL
# replaces L with the pair (id 5, R's own add, is skipped as in
# joycon-combine), and L's removal releases Space at @800. The pair is
# back under the key it had, and taps south.
# The GUIDs and serials are joycon-combine's; the pair has no serial, so
# its key is its GUID and fixed path.
